notes: "A slide alone does not tell the next editor what matters. HUANDENG keeps a short Story beside every slide: its purpose, what must be kept, and the change that was asked for. On the left is the Story tab from the editor. On the right is the Story I actually recorded for the 1BNA chart slide you just saw: keep the values exactly as in the CSV, keep a labelled non-zero axis with units, keep the citation, and make no claim of replicates or trends. When an AI agent is asked to tidy that slide, this is what it reads first. Story also exists for the whole project, for each Section and for each Presentation, so a change can be judged against the purpose of the talk as well as the slide. An agent's Story record is its interpretation of the request; it is not the author's approval."
